A||||9||Shaun41178||99 Trans Am vs. NOS Fiero
Z||000000||Shaun41178||05-11-99||03:54 AM||||Well I have finally got my first race out of the way. Its about freakin' time too. I thought it was never going to happen.<br>Tonight(Sun) I went over to a friends house and after leaving I thought I would go try and find some trouble although I had always been unsuccesful before. So I opened my Nitrous valve and off I went. <br>Waiting for traffic to clear so I can pull out I see a 4th Gen Black Firebird roll by. Several cars went by before a clearing of the traffic so I tried to spot the Firebird up ahead and see where it was going. Luckily he got caught at a light turning left so I pulled in behind him. Light turned green and I continued to follow and pulled up along side and put my nose in front of his and then I slowed down and then sped up again. He probably thought that I wanted to go right there so he dropped the hammer and sped off leaving me behind. He got caught at a light ahead and because I was doing the relative speed limit I timed the light perfectly and as I drove by I punched it to let him know that I was interested and we continued to go back and forth like this for a while but were unable to get a good race going cause a truck was trying to play as well. <br>I sped ahead to get the truck away from us and when the truck backed off the Firebird came flying by at about 80 mph. I just kept going the same pace cause I was doing about 60 when he sped by so there was no way that I was going to catch him.<br>Well the guy caught a light far ahead so I sped ahead so I could line up next to the guy. As I pull up along side i notice 30 day temp tags where the license plate goes. I roll down my window and I ask him if it is a 99? He says yes. Not knowing the f-bod style too well plus it being dark out I couldn't tell what kind but if I had to guess I would say it was a T/A with the LS1. I ask him and his buddy if he wants to give me a run and he says sure. He then says that he has to make a turn about an 1/8th mile up ahead so I said no problem it can just be a little race. I said that I would probably get spanked but at this point I didn't care. I just wanted to see one of these in action. I was pumped for this race. <br>Waiting for the light to turn green and being full of excitement I forgot to powerbrake. Light turned green and I just punched the nitrous right off idle. We both were barking the tires loudly, I am guessing he had a manual tranny cause he didn't have too great of traction. My car got a little sideways in the rear but corrected itself as I gained speed. The race only went about 250 feet or so before I let off cause the guys turn was quickly approaching but the tranny had hit second gear cause I was around 45-50 mph at the time. I looked in my drivers side mirror and saw his headlights and quickly glanced over my shoulder and saw that I was about a car and a half ahead of him. I don't know if he had started to gain on me or not before I shut down but none the less I was ahead. I would've beaten him to 60 but I am sure once he had traction he would've taken me easily.<br>Slowing down he pulled along side and waived and I gave him the thumbs up and he made his turn and I continued to go straight ahead.<br>So I guess this is a win but I will only call it a 1/2 win cause it was a relatively short race. Sorry for such a long post but I am just really excited to go up against an Ls-1 for my first ever race and pull ahead of it like i did. <br>------------------<br>2.8V6 3.08 FD 3 spd auto <br>Crane HI6S ignition <br>PS-91 Coil<br>Accel 8.8 mm wires<br>NOS 70 hp shot<br>Future mods: Hi lift cam full port and polish of heads and intake<br>Currently 130 hp @ wheels <br>Without Nitrous<br>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178
Z||000001||LEE498||05-11-99||09:57 AM||||Way to go!!! SHAUN That make's me proud to hear an fiero whup some asss like that, keep up the good work! Don't worry about a long post any time someone has a whup ass story to tell, just tell it! ANY BODY ELSE GOT A WHUP ASS STORY???? 
Z||000002||Patrick||05-11-99||04:36 PM||||<br>Ah yes, to be young again. Thanks Shaun for bringing back memories from 25 years ago. (Gawd, has it been THAT long!!!)<p>I'm sure that this is the longest post you've submitted anywhere in a long time. Maybe even the longest ever. Isn't it amazing what inspires us?<p><b>No wonder women don't understand us. :)</b><p>
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||05-13-99||07:57 PM||||  I have an 86 SE V6. I have had the car since 89 and have never modified it other than a K&N filter. Back when i cruised the streets, looking for trouble, i have surprised many folks. Among the victems are Mustangs(many),camaros and the such.Once a Grand National. The GN sticks out in my mind the most. It belonged to a guy i knew, but not personally. I was driving down the street when this black car pulls along side. I got nervous and decided to see what might happen so i sped up to show intent. Then I heard the tubo spooling on the GN. I went to third and i sped up but he blew past me.If I knew then that second gear at 30 mph is much much better. At the next light i asked to go from a dead stop, he said alright.I saw the opposite light turn yellow and i tached it to 2500 and he was power braking to build boost. Our light turned green and we took off. Before the race he said the first to 60 wins. I pulled ahead and was very surprised i did so. Then i shifted and he caught me and then i started to pull ahead again. Then i shifted to third and didn't loose any ground. By 60 mph I was a car length ahead. When we stopped he asked me the question i would hear many times in the near future. "What is in that thing?" I didn't realize what i had at the time(and not really sure now) but it is very fast. I ran the car at the local track and i posted a 14.7 second 1/4 mile time and hit 98 mph.
Z||000004||Eric||05-13-99||08:24 PM||||Wow! 14.7 at 98 mph.  I wish I had your engine in my car, it would save me a lot of time and money in a 3.1 rebuild.<p>You aren't related to Crowell, are you?
Z||000005||LEE498||05-13-99||08:56 PM||||WHAT THA F-CK!!!!! 14.7 at 98mph ,where did you get that filter??? Whewww!!! man your car is VERY FAST! You got to be pumping about 200hp. Well i'll tell you what,that car can't be stock.Hmmmm, maybe a 3.1's in there. By the way your name ain't cowell is it?????? 
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||05-13-99||09:37 PM||||Who is Crowell? The car has a very distinct sound like no other fiero and i'm corious as to what could be done to it too. I live in Utah and we have to pass emissions here and i pass easy. I have never had a break down so i have never peeked inside the engine to see anything done to it. Maybe some porting or something? Maybe a 3.1 crank but i don't think it was being done in the years before i got it. I plan on transplanting this mill to a better car and doing a rebuild to stop that annoying leak and maybe i can find any mods. By the way who is Crowell?
